--TEST--
PHP's enum members are refused where they are written: `->name`, `->value`, `cases`, `from`, `tryFrom`, a method in the body and an `implements` clause — `rule:enums/no-class-machinery`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:enums/what-replaces-php-s-enum-members
enum Level { Debug, Info }

// `rule:enums/no-class-machinery`: an enum is a closed set of integers rather
// than a class, so it implements nothing and declares no member of its own.
enum Ranked implements Countable { Low, High }

enum Spoken {
    Yes,
    No,
    public static function label(): string { return "yes"; }
}

// A case is a compile-time integer, so it carries no property: `->value` is
// `as int` and `->name` is a `match` in a class that takes the enum.
Level $held = Level::Info;
echo $held->name, "\n";
echo $held->value, "\n";

// The three static members PHP puts on a backed enum. `cases` is a static
// method of your own, `from` is `$n as Level` and `tryFrom` is `$n as ?Level`.
Level::cases();
Level::from(1);
Level::tryFrom(1);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0218]: an enum cannot implement an interface
%A
error[E0220]: an enum declares only cases and an optional backing type
%A
error[E0405]: `Level` has no property named `name`
%A
error[E0405]: `Level` has no property named `value`
%A
error[E0309]: `Level` has no method named `cases`
%A
error[E0309]: `Level` has no method named `from`
%A
error[E0309]: `Level` has no method named `tryFrom`
%A
error: aborting due to 7 errors
